UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): A dual-purpose test simultaneously addresses two objectives: evaluating whether a control is operating effectively (test of controls) and detecting material misstatements in an amount or disclosure (substantive test). Under AU-C 330, inspecting a purchase order for an authorized signature tests the control while verifying the recorded amount tests the assertion.
Wrong (A): This describes testing the same assertion with multiple procedures, not a dual-purpose test that combines control and substantive objectives.
Wrong (B): Dual-purpose tests apply different objectives to the same item, not the same procedure to two different accounts.
