-- Q7592: Specific Areas and Transactions [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under AU-C 501, when the auditor observes physical inventory, the auditor performs test counts and then traces those counts to the final inventory compilation. This step ensures that quantities observed were accurately reflected in the records used to value inventory.
Wrong (A): Observation alone is insufficient; the auditor must verify that physical count results are properly incorporated into the final inventory listing.
Wrong (B): Recalculating all extensions is not required and goes beyond the purpose of tracing test counts to the final listing.
Wrong (D): There is no concept of an inventory certificate issued by the auditor based solely on test counts; the auditor provides an opinion on the financial statements as a whole.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 7592;

-- Q7593: Specific Areas and Transactions [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under AU-C 570, the auditor must assess whether management''s plans are feasible and can be effectively implemented. A conditional credit facility with unmet conditions does not adequately alleviate substantial doubt, so the auditor should conclude doubt remains and evaluate whether disclosures are adequate.
Wrong (A): A conditional commitment with unmet requirements does not provide sufficient mitigation of going concern uncertainty; willingness alone is not a binding commitment.
Wrong (B): An adverse opinion indicates the financial statements are materially misstated, which is not the issue here; going concern doubt calls for an emphasis-of-matter paragraph, not an adverse opinion.
Wrong (C): Withdrawal is not required when management''s plan is insufficient; the auditor evaluates disclosures and modifies the report as appropriate.$EXPL$
