-- Q7595: Specific Areas and Transactions [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): This describes check kiting--recording an interbank transfer deposit before it actually occurs to inflate the cash balance. The disbursement from Bank A on December 30 is properly recorded, but the deposit into Bank B was not made until January 3, making the December 30 deposit entry an overstatement of $275,000. Under AU-C 330, auditors test bank transfers near year-end to detect kiting.
Wrong (A): The disbursement was recorded on the date the check was drawn, which is proper; it is the deposit side that is misstated.
Wrong (B): The physical deposit did not occur until January 3, so recording both on December 30 does not make the balance correct.
Wrong (D): Only the deposit side is misstated; the disbursement was properly recorded, so the overstatement is $275,000, not $550,000.$EXPL$
