-- Q7613: Specific Areas and Transactions [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under AU-C 330, the extent of substantive procedures (sample size) directly affects detection risk. A smaller sample provides less evidence, increasing the probability that the auditor will fail to detect a material misstatement that exists.
Wrong (A): Thoroughness of examining individual items does not offset the reduced population coverage; detection risk depends on how much of the population is tested.
Wrong (B): Inherent risk is a characteristic of the entity and its transactions, not a function of the auditor''s procedures or sample size.
Wrong (C): Control risk is assessed based on the design and operating effectiveness of internal controls, not adjusted to compensate for the auditor''s sample size decisions.$EXPL$
