-- Q7614: Specific Areas and Transactions [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AU-C 540, the auditor must evaluate indicators of possible management bias, including patterns where management consistently selects estimates at one end of the reasonable range. While each individual estimate may be reasonable, the cumulative effect of consistently selecting the low end across multiple estimates may result in a material misstatement of the financial statements taken as a whole.
Wrong (B): Ignoring the pattern across multiple estimates violates the requirement to assess bias; reasonableness of individual estimates does not preclude cumulative misstatement.
Wrong (C): Requiring midpoint adjustments for all estimates is arbitrary; the auditor evaluates whether the pattern indicates bias, not mandates specific point estimates.
Wrong (D): A qualified opinion requires a material misstatement or scope limitation; selecting the low end of one range, standing alone, does not necessarily warrant qualification.$EXPL$
